From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xaver Hugl
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:53:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] scene/workspacescene: don't let hidden items occlude anything
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

addOpaqueRegionRecursive() doesn't check visibility, so hidden items
still count as opaque in the occlusion cull pass of
WorkspaceScene::collectDamage(). A cached QuickSceneEffect view is
hidden but stays in the overlay, and since QuickSceneView has no alpha
channel its whole rect is opaque. After closing a cached effect once,
all window damage on that output gets culled and windows stop
repainting.

An item that isn't visible isn't painted, so it can't occlude
anything. Skip hidden items and their children, matching how
painting treats them.


(cherry picked from commit 62222dbf2474439a905959cb5d63a60171d97086)

Co-authored-by: Rafał Domecki

Carried unchanged, applied with a 55-line offset (the stereo depth code sits above). The edition's own
addSolidRegionRecursive, which clears the eye passes below culling windows (ORDER 319), already skips
items that are not explicitly visible, so only addOpaqueRegionRecursive needed the check.

Origin: upstream, https://invent.kde.org/plasma/kwin/-/commit/37d327ce46b09fadd722d19812d2481dcbdd0a40
Author: Xaver Hugl
Applied-Upstream: v6.7.6, 37d327ce46 (Plasma/6.7), 62222dbf24 (master)
Last-Update: 2026-11-07

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
 src/scene/workspacescene.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/scene/workspacescene.cpp b/src/scene/workspacescene.cpp
index 571948e9fa..2dbe2b1782 100644
--- a/src/scene/workspacescene.cpp
+++ b/src/scene/workspacescene.cpp
@@ -603,6 +603,9 @@ void WorkspaceScene::preparePaintGenericScreen()
 
 static void addOpaqueRegionRecursive(SceneView *view, Item *item, const std::optional<ClipCorner> &parentCorner, Region &ret)
 {
+    if (!item->isVisible()) {
+        return;
+    }
     const std::optional<ClipCorner> corner = calculateClipCorner(item, parentCorner);
     RegionF opaque = item->opaque();
     if (corner.has_value()) {
